msgstr ""

#: ../../source/psl_README.md:15
msgid "What is the Public Suffix List?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/psl_README.md:17
msgid ""
"The Public Suffix List is a cross-vendor initiative to provide an "
"accurate list of domain name suffixes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/psl_README.md:20
msgid ""
"The Public Suffix List is an initiative of the Mozilla Project, but is "
"maintained as a community resource. It is available for use in any "
"software, but was originally created to meet the needs of browser "
"manufacturers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/psl_README.md:24
msgid ""
"A \"public suffix\" is one under which Internet users can directly "
"register names. Some examples of public suffixes are \".com\", \".co.uk\""
" and \"pvt.k12.wy.us\". The Public Suffix List is a list of all known "
"public suffixes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/psl_README.md:28
msgid "Source: http://publicsuffix.org"
msgstr ""

